{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPoZ6xgxosL6LBNGkXnY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a ROS 2 (Robot Operating System 2) issue. They have:\n1. A publisher on `/camera/image_raw` that's publishing at 30 Hz (verified by `ros2 topic hz`)\n2. A subscriber that never receives messages\n3. Code compiles fine and the node starts\n\nThis is a classic ROS 2 debugging scenario. There are several common causes:\n\n1. **QoS (Quality of Service) mismatch** - This is the most common issue. The publisher and subscriber need compatible QoS settings. For example, if the publisher uses `KEEP_LAST(1)` with depth 1, and the subscriber uses `KEEP_LAST(10)`, they might not match.\n\n2. **Callback never being called** - The subscriber might be created, but the callback isn't being invoked because the node isn't spinning/running the executor.\n\n3. **Topic namespace mismatch** - Maybe the publisher and subscriber are in different namespaces.\n\n4. **Message type mismatch** - The publisher and subscriber are subscribing to different message types.\n\n5. **Node not being spun** - The most common issue: the subscriber node isn't calling `rclpy.spin()` or using an executor.\n\nWithout seeing the actual code, I should ask clarifying questions to help them debug. But based on typical patterns, the most likely issues are:\n\n1. Node not spinning (callback thread not running)\n2. QoS mismatch\n3. Callback not actually being called due to issues in the callback setup\n\nI should ask to see their code to diagnose the issue properly. Let me provide some common causes and ask to see the subscriber code.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6552,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6552},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e3c7f50-92a5-40be-bcc0-983779869383","uuid":"5102d94c-ea8f-4631-a878-40e66a61c61d","timestamp":"2026-07-26T01:30:08.497Z","request_id":"req_011CdPoZ5riKchtrPT7Uiv6V"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPoZ6xgxosL6LBNGkXnY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The most common cause is that your subscriber's **callback is never being invoked** because the node isn't spinning. Here are the likely culprits in order:\n\n1. **Node not spinning** — The subscriber callback only fires when you call `rclpy.spin()` or run an executor. If your code creates the subscription but doesn't spin, no callbacks execute.\n\n2. **QoS mismatch** — Publisher and subscriber QoS profiles must be compatible. If the publisher uses `KEEP_LAST(1)` with depth 1 but the subscriber uses stricter settings (or vice versa), they won't connect.\n\n3. **Callback issue** — The callback exists but crashes silently or never gets wired up.\n\nCan you share your subscriber code? Specifically:\n- How are you creating the subscription? \n- Are you calling `rclpy.spin()` or using an executor?\n- What QoS settings (if any) are you using for both publisher and subscriber?\n\nIn the meantime, verify QoS with:\n```bash\nros2 topic info /camera/image_raw --verbose\n```\n\nThis shows both publisher and subscriber QoS profiles. If they don't match, that's your issue—add `qos_profile=rclpy.qos.QoSPresetProfiles.SENSOR_DATA` to the subscription (or whatever profile the publisher uses)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6552,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6552},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e3c7f50-92a5-40be-bcc0-983779869383","uuid":"6fb7efbd-fe90-4968-92d4-9b1cbbd0c717","timestamp":"2026-07-26T01:30:11.749Z","request_id":"req_011CdPoZ5riKchtrPT7Uiv6V"}
